complex dimension 1: c_1 = 0 only for degree [3] in CP^2; c(TX) = 1 J^0 + 0 J^1; chi = 0 * 3 = 0
complex dimension 2: c_1 = 0 only for degree [4] in CP^3; c(TX) = 1 J^0 + 0 J^1 + 6 J^2; chi = 6 * 4 = 24
complex dimension 3: c_1 = 0 only for degree [5] in CP^4; c(TX) = 1 J^0 + 0 J^1 + 10 J^2 + -40 J^3; chi = -40 * 5 = -200
complex dimension 4: c_1 = 0 only for degree [6] in CP^5; c(TX) = 1 J^0 + 0 J^1 + 15 J^2 + -70 J^3 + 435 J^4; chi = 435 * 6 = 2610
the cubic curve is a torus (chi = 0), the quartic is K3 (chi = 24), the quintic has chi = -200, the sextic fourfold chi = 2610
